WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.770
 Somewhere along
this journey, you

00:00:01.770 --> 00:00:05.916
may see some personality
quirks that are weird.

00:00:05.916 --> 00:00:08.115
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:08.115 --> 00:00:10.490
Every scene in a movie is
trying to accomplish something.

00:00:10.490 --> 00:00:13.940
Do all the things that
you have in your mind that

00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:16.820
will inform the audience
when they see this character.

00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:19.490
Oh, that's who that is.

00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:21.440
After taking this
class, you will

00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:24.680
be able to walk into a room,
present your best self,

00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:28.740
and be happy with the result.

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:31.290
We are living in a
world of make believe.

00:00:31.290 --> 00:00:32.479
So make it up.

00:00:32.479 --> 00:00:34.850
When you're at home
preparing, you break down

00:00:34.850 --> 00:00:36.380
what he's trying to convey--

00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:38.430
the person he's speaking
to and to the audience.

00:00:38.430 --> 00:00:41.990
The truth is, it's
who you are inflicted

00:00:41.990 --> 00:00:44.750
upon the truth of the
dialogue that's written there.

00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:46.880
And we all have comfort zones.

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:49.280
The hard work,
sometimes, as an actor

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:52.370
is getting out of
your comfort zone.

00:00:52.370 --> 00:00:55.760
If you have a personal biography
for your character, that's

00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:57.570
a way to get inside
of it and figure out,

00:00:57.570 --> 00:00:59.450
you know, why does
he talk this way?

00:00:59.450 --> 00:01:00.106
Is he a loner?

00:01:00.106 --> 00:01:00.980
Does he have friends?

00:01:00.980 --> 00:01:03.560
Is he a cynic?

00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:07.220
Learn what acting techniques
are in other cultures.

00:01:07.220 --> 00:01:09.710
You might find it more
interesting than the way

00:01:09.710 --> 00:01:11.840
we normally do it.

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:14.180
In an audition,
don't say to them,

00:01:14.180 --> 00:01:17.990
I don't think my character would
do that because your character

00:01:17.990 --> 00:01:19.890
won't do that because
you won't be hired,

00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:21.390
and you won't be
getting that check.

00:01:25.180 --> 00:01:27.490
I made a decision
early in my life

00:01:27.490 --> 00:01:31.300
that I wasn't gonna live and
die in Chattanooga, Tennessee.

00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:35.980
Being able to embody a lot of
different characters in film

00:01:35.980 --> 00:01:39.010
has been very cathartic,
being able to let

00:01:39.010 --> 00:01:42.250
go of the anger or
the disappointment

00:01:42.250 --> 00:01:45.470
that I had in my life.

00:01:45.470 --> 00:01:47.150
Essentially, we're entertainers.

00:01:47.150 --> 00:01:48.850
Find a way to make
yourself special.

00:01:48.850 --> 00:01:51.530
Give it something that
will distract people

00:01:51.530 --> 00:01:53.720
from their daily
lives in a way that

00:01:53.720 --> 00:01:57.240
allows them to live in this
moment with us for a while

00:01:57.240 --> 00:02:01.790
and leave there energized
by it and love it.

00:02:01.790 --> 00:02:06.910
I'm Samuel L. Jackson, and
this is my MasterClass.

